    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/05/asics-metaspeed-edge-tokyo-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: FF Leap creates a very soft, bouncy forefoot with strong impact absorption, while the FF Turbo+ heel feels firmer and stable without feeling harsh on landing.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is highly energetic and snappy, with strong bounce/energy return from FF Leap and a quick transition driven by the spooned plate; the 5.9 oz weight further boosts fast-pace feel.",
        "Stability: Heel stability is notably improved by added sole flare and a rearfoot bucket sensation; carbon-plated stiffness and strong upper lockdown reduce slippage, though the very soft forefoot is only moderately stable laterally.",
        "Durability: Durability is expected to be above average; the lightweight mesh held structure well under load and outsole grip was good on roads, but long-term outsole wear was not yet fully established."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/07/asics-metaspeed-edge-tokyo-review-2.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The dual-foam midsole blends softer FF Leap above the plate with firmer FF Turbo Plus below it; forefoot feels softer/more rockered while the heel feels firmer and protective.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is described as light, poppy, and efficient, with cadence increasing about 2-4 spm at the same pace (190 to 194), showing strong turnover/snappiness from the aggressive plate angle.",
        "Stability: A firmer lower foam plus the plate geometry gave stable cornering, and the reviewer noted a comfortable heel lock with secure support on roads.",
        "Durability: Outsole grip performance was strong (including wet uphill roads), but long-term wear was not fully documented; the main material concern was midsole foam absorbing water/sweat and getting heavier/sloshy in wet or hot conditions."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/asics-metaspeed-edge-tokyo-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: FF Leap makes the ride noticeably softer and more forgiving, with strong forefoot cushioning and better impact smoothing than prior Metaspeed versions.",
        "Responsiveness: The FF Leap + FF Turbo+ + carbon plate setup delivers a lively bounce and clear propulsive toe-off, making pace lock-in feel easier at speed.",
        "Stability: For a race shoe it feels relatively stable due to firmer foam under the plate and a stiffened platform, though the low collar/limited ankle structure and reported heel lift reduce rearfoot security.",
        "Durability: Asicsgrip outsole is highlighted for strong grip in wet turns and varied conditions, but the review provides little long-term wear data on outsole or upper longevity."
      ]
    }
